<title>BRAZIL: Coffee quotas make sense in 1997/98 - Brazil trade.</title>
<headline>Coffee quotas make sense in 1997/98 - Brazil trade.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A decision by the Association of Coffee Producing Countries (ACPC) to continue export quotas through to June 1998 makes sense given expectations of a bumper Brazil crop in 1998/99, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;As long as the crops are small, the export quotas will work. And this can hold in 1997/98,&quot; onler said. &quot;But by September/October with the first rains, people will start to get an idea of the Brazilian new crop size and expectation alone is enough to drive the market down,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
